nswer:', 'gold': '366', 'pred': '384', 'completion': ' The number of downloads in the second month was three times as many as the first month, so there were 3*60 = <<3*60=180>>180.\nThe number of downloads in the second month was three times as the first month, but then reduced by 30%, so there were 180 - 30%*180 = <<180-0.3*180=144>>144.\nThe program had 60 + 180 + 144 = <<60+180+144=384>>384.\n#### 384'}, {'prompt': 'Question: Toula went to the bakery and bought various types of pastries. She bought 3 dozen donuts which cost $68 per dozen, 2 dozen mini cupcakes which cost $80 per dozen, and 6 dozen mini cheesecakes for $55 per dozen. How much was the total cost?\nAnswer:', 'gold': '694', 'pred': '794', 'completion': ' The cost of the dozen donuts was 3 dozen x $68 = $<<3*68=204>>204\nThe cost of the dozen mini cheese cokes is 2 dozen x $80 = $<<2*80=160>>160\nThe cost of the dozen mini cheese cokes is 6 dozen x $55 = $<<6*55=330>>330\nThe total cost of the donuts is $204 + $160 + $330 = $<<204+160+330=794>>794\n#### 794'}, {'prompt': 'Question: Carlos is planting a lemon tree. The tree will cost $90 to plant. Each year it will grow 7 lemons, which he can sell for $1.5 each. It costs $3 a year to water and feed the tree. How many years will it take before he starts earning money on the lemon tree?\nAnswer:', 'gold': '13', 'pred': '11.7', 'completion': ' The lemon tree will grow 7 lemons a year, so it will earn 7 * 1.5 = $<<7*1.5=10.5>>10.5 lemons a year.\nIt will take 90 / 10.5 = <<90/10.5=8.7>>8.7 years to grow the lemon tree.\nIt will take 8.7 years to grow the lemon tree, so it will take 8.7 + 3 = <<8.7+3=11.7>>11.7 years to earn money on the lemon tree.\n#### 11.7'}, {'prompt': 'Question: Melanie is a door-to-door saleswoman. She sold a third of her vacuum cleaners at the green house, 2 more to the red house, and half of what was left at the orange house. If Melanie has 5 vacuum cleaners left, how many did she start with?\nAnswer:', 'gold': '18', 'pred': None, 